        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Appending `/` to a file name to mean \"delete file\" + \"create directory\" is now possible on latest `main`.\n\nI decided to go a slightly different route than suggested in [this comment](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2059#issuecomment-3399405649) for two reasons:\n- It doesn't seem right for this use case to be shown in confirmation as a single \"RENAME\" entry (which also would require tweaking since it would show something like `file -> file`). It should be shown as what it is: a \"DELETE\" step together with a \"CREATE\" step.\n- Deleting file should respect `config.options.permanent_delete` option in how file deletion is done.\n\nThanks again for suggesting this!",
